<title>BELGIUM: FINNISH INDUSTRY WANTS EMU, HAMALAINEN SAYS.</title>
<headline>FINNISH INDUSTRY WANTS EMU, HAMALAINEN SAYS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Finland governor Sirkka Hamalainen said on Tuesday Finnish industry was strongly in favour of the EU's planned economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;It is very clear; the whole industry in Finland is supportive of EMU,&quot; Hamalainen told the European Parliament's monetary committee.</p>
<p>Hamalainen also said Finland supports the proposal for a stability pact to ensure fiscal discipline for countries in the euro-zone.</p>
<p>She said she wanted to see a &quot;strict&quot; system but that flexibility was also needed.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
